hes US government official communications to use the term 'super intelligence'.", "likely_countermove": "Senator Bernie Sanders and Representative Greg Casar pursue the passage of the Ban Artificial Superintelligence Act.", "mechanism": "The President announces the US government will rename AI 'super intelligence' in official communications -> Legislators introduce a bill to ban artificial superintelligence -> US official documents face conflicting legislative and executive terminology regarding AI.", "narrowed_from": {"original_blockers": [], "original_grounding": {"mechanism": "partially_supported", "thesis": "inference_supported"}, "thesis": "The simultaneous executive rebranding of all AI as 'super intelligence' and legislative efforts to outlaw 'artificial superintelligence' creates a profound statutory collision. Without precise technical benchmarking, standard AI procurement by federal agencies could be functionally paralyzed by conflicting nomenclature mandates.", "what_was_narrowed": "Removed unsupported claims regarding procurement paralysis, legal uncertainty, and strategic leverage to reflect only the documented conflicting executive renaming and legislative ban proposals."}, "novel_proposition": "Executive terminology changes for AI directly overlap with proposed legislative naming in banned technology bills.", "promotion_blockers": [], "quality_origin": "strategic-hypothesis-lab-v1.6-blind-user-hypotheses", "research_question": "", "resolved_evidence_ids": ["EVID-5AB3DE7E822691295FEBB259", "EVID-F267DE49228B0EF3F47F4CD2", "EVID-1E5DEBA526FD1A9DE74ED745", "EVID-50B4751B2FF93A272082C4A2"], "second_order_effect": "", "source_ids": ["B1H1", "B2H2"], "status": "verified", "supporting_evidence": [{"credibility": "unrated source", "date": "", "evidence_id": "EVID-5AB3DE7E822691295FEBB259", "publisher": "yahoo.com", "text": "President Donald Trump on Tuesday announced that the US government would rename artificial intelligence \"super intelligence\" in officia