UyUD37OS-VKElo3CyN29i6eN_p3HA4fCsG6bUiK04vJITqpk_18Bjf3aC40y4hiZfqaZz5fRLSBAx9Lg8uY6DIK7AA="}, "round": 1}], "usage": {"accepted_evidence_records": 0, "duplicate_or_redundant_records": 0, "elapsed_seconds": 89.87897419999354, "grounding_reassessments": 0, "independent_corroborations": 0, "materially_new_evidence_records": 0, "planner_calls": 1, "queries_executed": 6, "queries_planned": 6, "reported_estimated_cost": 0.0, "reported_input_tokens": 0, "reported_output_tokens": 0, "reported_total_tokens": 0, "search_results_seen": 12, "search_rounds": 1, "sources_fetched": 1}}, "evidence": [], "history": {"limitations": ["analogical_mechanism: free_providers: failed", "direct_precedent: free_providers: failed", "result not reviewed (source_fetch_budget_exhausted)"], "note": "Retrieved comparisons are not a representative reference class. Do not infer a base rate by counting these news examples.", "records": [], "status": "searched"}, "insight_id": "LAB-EV2", "searched_hypothesis": {"alternative_explanations": ["The delay was purely a technical forensic failure stemming from the novel difficulty of identifying autonomous agent actions within massive server logs, completely independent of EU compliance prioritization."], "counterevidence_ids": [], "critical_unknowns": ["Did the AI provider report any systemic risk incidents to the EU Commission 'without undue delay' during the exact same three-month period they delayed reporting the breach to Australia?", "Evidence emerges that the AI provider simultaneously delayed reporting similarly severe systemic risk incidents to the EU Commission despite the threat of the 3% fine."], "insight": "The months-long delay in notifying mid-tier governments of autonomous AI breaches is a byproduct of global regulatory arbitrage, where AI providers triage their limited forensic telemetry resources to satisfy jurisdictions imposing severe revenue-based fines, leaving states with strict timelines but weaker penalties structurally blind.", "insight_id": "LAB-EV2", "insight_type": "prospective", "mechanism": {"description": "The EU implements severe 3% global turnover fines for AI incidents -> AI providers prioritize forensic reviews and compliance reporting to satisfy EU mandates -> Incident discovery and reporting for jurisdictions lacking similar financial teeth (like Australia) is delayed by months."}, "metadata": {"lens": "regulatory arbitrage or policy feedback", "novel_proposition": "Global AI safety incidents are currently reported based on the financial severity of the jurisdiction's penalties rather than the technical severity of the incident or local 12-to-72 hour mandates.", "origin": "strategic-hypothesis-lab-v1.6-blind-user-hypotheses", "why_not_obvious": "An unprecedented AI hack on a government network should theoretically trigger an immediate maximum-priority alert; the 3-month delay reveals that AI model telemetry review is a bottlenecked resource allocated by compliance risk."}, "premises": [{"evidence_ids": ["EVID-C2A4F05609A8DF3032E36EDE"], "premise_id": "LAB-P-F7", "premise_type": "factual", "text": "(At the UN Wednesday Australian Prime Minister Anthony Albanese complained it took three months for OpenAI to then alert Australia's government about the breach, Bloomberg reports .)"}, {"evidence_ids": ["EVID-65CFAEF5390DEF6D131BE273"], "premise_id": "LAB-P-F11", "premise_type": "factual", "text": "Article 55 of the AI Act has obliged providers of general-purpose models with systemic risk to run adversarial testing, assess risk at union level and report serious incidents without undue delay since August 2025."}, {"evidence_ids": ["EVID-52B4FF635215A384AF63E0FF", "EVID-0476EACE53022E410008ABA8", "EVID-697F5CA02E3A1BA05D6F8242"], "premise_id": "LAB-P-F12", "premise_type": "factual", "text": "The European Union has required them since August 2025, and since 2 August this year the Commission has been able to fine a model provider 3% of worldwide turnover."}, {"evidence_ids": ["EVID-7F245C8DCFCBC6762E9746F4", "EVID-86552ACB7912E78EFB41C631"], "premise_id": "LAB-P-F19", "premise_type": "factual", "text": "Within these organisations, if you become aware that a critical cyber security incident has occurred or is occurring, AND the incident has had, or is having, a significant impact on the availability of your asset, you must notify ACSC within 12 hours after you become aware of the incident."}, {"evidence_ids": ["EVID-86552ACB7912E78EFB41C631", "EVID-7F245C8DCFCBC6762E9746F4"], "premise_id": "LAB-P-F20", "premise_type": "factual", "text": "If you become aware that a cyber security incident has occurred or is occurring, AND the incident has had, is having, or is likely to have, a relevant impact on your asset, you must notify ACSC within 72 hours after you become aware of the incident."}], "second_order_effect": "Mid-tier nations will be forced to rapidly adopt European-style, revenue-based extraterritorial fine models simply to secure timely intelligence on their own domestic cyber breaches.", "supporting_evidence_ids": ["EVID-C2A4F05609A8DF3032E36EDE", "EVID-65CFAEF5390DEF6D131BE273", "EVID-52B4FF635215A384AF63E0FF", "EVID-7F245C8DCFCBC6762E9746F4", "EVID-86552ACB7912E78EFB41C631", "EVID-0476EACE53022E410008ABA8", "EVID-697F5CA02E3A1BA05D6F8242"]}, "seed_evidence_ids": ["EVID-C2A4F05609A8DF3032E36EDE", "EVID-65CFAEF5390DEF6D131BE273", "EVID-52B4FF635215A384AF63E0FF", "EVID-7F245C8DCFCBC6762E9746F4", "EVID-86552ACB7912E78EFB41C631", "EVID-0476EACE53022E410008ABA8", "EVID-697F5CA02E3A1BA05D6F8242"], "source_documents": {}, "version": "hypothesis-evidence-v1.1"}, {"as_of": "2026-10-23T07:03:04.642892+00:00", "assessment": {"completeness": "incomplete", "families": {"challenge": {"blockers": ["analogical_mechanism: a fetched source could not be reviewed", "feasibility: a fetched source could not be reviewed"], "limitations": ["alternative_explanation: a found source could not be fetched", "alternative_explanation: gdelt: RATE_LIMITED", "alternative_explanat