D49479C92BD", "event_keys": ["claim_status", "created_at", "entity_mentions", "event_dates_version", "event_end_at", "event_id", "event_start_at", "event_time_text", "event_type", "extraction_metadata", "published_at", "quantitative_claims", "relationship_mentions", "snippets", "source_id", "strategic_admission_reasons", "strategic_admission_status", "strategic_cluster_check", "strategic_cluster_development", "strategic_cluster_id", "strategic_cluster_label", "strategic_cluster_status", "strategic_cluster_terms", "strategic_dependency_tags", "strategic_event_class", "strategic_geography", "strategic_materiality_score", "strategic_mechanism_tags", "strategic_relation_signature", "strategic_theme", "strategic_time_window", "strategic_topic_linkage_type", "strategic_topic_relevance_score", "summary", "temporal_precision", "temporal_status", "title", "underlying_event_id", "underlying_event_member_count", "updated_at"], "event_summary": "One of OpenAI's first country partnerships is with the United Arab Emirates, where homosexuality is illegal and criticism of the government is forbidden.", "raw_actor_fields": {"acting_entity": null, "actor": null, "company": null, "institution": null, "organisation": null, "organization": null, "primary_actor": null, "regulator": null}, "raw_entity_mentions": [{"entity_type": "organization", "mention": "OpenAI", "raw_keys": ["context", "entity_type", "mention", "role", "sentence_id", "source_span", "type_source"], "role": "actor"}, {"entity_type": "unknown", "mention": "United Arab Emirates", "raw_keys": ["context", "entity_type", "mention", "role", "sentence_id", "source_span", "type_source"], "role": "object"}], "resolved_primary_actor": "OpenAI", "source_id": "SOURCE-68E783C62BEACFA9BF64436C"}, {"admission_reasons": [], "admission_status": "considered", "diagnostic_version": "strategic-actor-admission-diagnostics-v1", "entity_mentions_state": "present", "event_id": "EVENT-4AEC46E36F4A76B97A2B7E33", "event_keys": ["claim_status", "created_at", "entity_mentions", "event_dates_version", "event_end_at", "event_id", "event_start_at", "event_time_text", "event_type", "extraction_metadata", "published_at", "quantitative_claims", "relationship_mentions", "snippets", "source_id", "strategic_admission_reasons", "strategic_admission_status", "strategic_cluster_check", "strategic_cluster_development", "strategic_cluster_id", "strategic_cluster_label", "strategic_cluster_status", "strategic_cluster_terms", "strategic_dependency_tags", "strategic_event_class", "strategic_geography", "strategic_materiality_score", "strategic_mechanism_tags", "strategic_relation_signature", "strategic_theme", "strategic_time_window", "strategic_topic_linkage_type", "strategic_topic_relevance_score", "summary", "temporal_precision", "temporal_status", "title", "underlying_event_id", "underlying_event_member_count", "updated_at"], "event_summary": "But earlier this year, the Meta Oversight Board found that five widely used models from Anthropic, Google, and OpenAI were more likely to refuse queries related to repressive governments. The board found that models were less willing to create a pamphlet criticizing the king of Thailand, which has lèse-majesté laws, than Charles III of England, which doesn't.", "raw_actor_fields": {"acting_entity": null, "actor": null, "company": null, "institution": null, "organisation": null, "organization": null, "primary_actor": null, "regulator": null}, "raw_entity_mentions": [{"entity_type": "organization", "mention": "Meta Oversight Board", "raw_keys": ["context", "entity_type", "mention", "role", "sentence_id", "source_span", "type_source"], "role": "actor"}, {"entity_type": "unknown", "mention": "five widely used models from Anthropic, Google, and OpenAI", "raw_keys": ["context", "entity_type", "mention", "role", "sentence_id", "source_span", "type_source"], "role": "object"}], "resolved_primary_actor": "Meta Oversight Board", "source_id": "SOURCE-68E783C62BEACFA9BF64436C"}, {"admission_reasons": [], "admission_status": "considered", "diagnostic_version": "strategic-actor-admission-diagnostics-v1", "entity_mentions_state": "present", "event_id": "EVENT-506B25A9DE398839C82B55C7", "event_keys": ["claim_status", "created_at", "entity_mentions", "event_dates_version", "event_end_at", "event_id", "event_start_at", "event_time_text", "event_type", "extraction_metadata", "published_at", "quantitative_claims", "relationship_mentions", "snippets", "source_id", "strategic_admission_reasons", "strategic_admission_status", "strategic_cluster_check", "strategic_cluster_development", "strategic_cluster_id", "strategic_cluster_label", "strategic_cluster_status", "strategic_cluster_terms", "strategic_dependency_tags", "strategic_event_class", "strategic_geography", "strategic_materiality_score", "strategic_mechanism_tags", "strategic_relation_signature", "strategic_theme", "strategic_time_window", "strategic_topic_linkage_type", "strategic_topic_relevance_score", "summary", "temporal_precision", "temporal_status", "title", "underlying_event_id", "underlying_event_member_count", "updated_at"], "event_summary": "Last winter, the UK AI Security Institute found that Anthropic models sometimes refused to assist in certain tasks related to AI safety research. Yet three of them refused more than half of what Anthropic called \"a set of reasonable AI safety research tasks.\"", "raw_actor_fields": {"acting_entity": null, "actor": null, "company": null, "institution": null, "organisation": null, "organization": null, "primary_actor": null, "regulator": null}, "raw_entity_mentions": [{"entity_type": "organization", "mention": "UK AI Security Institute", "raw_keys": ["context", "entity_type", "mention", "role", "sentence_id", "source_span", "type_source"], "role": "actor"}, {"entity_type": "unknown", "mention": "Anthropic models", "raw_keys": ["context", "entity_type", "mention", "role", "sentence_id", "source_span", "type_source"], "role": "object"}], "resolved_primary_actor": "