-event synthesis", "rank": 2, "ranked_by": "pairwise", "raw_score": 10, "ref": "strategic_hypotheses.verified[0]", "score": 10, "score_cap": 12, "strategic_type": "cross_event", "substance": {"added_inference": "The executive terminology move directly creates conflicting operational and legal terminology across government branches.", "adds_information": true, "alternative_explanation": "The executive announcement and legislative bill operate independently without causing legal conflict.", "bridge_supported": true, "complete": true, "decision_change": "Informs legal and policy compliance monitoring regarding official technology terminology definitions.", "discriminating_evidence": "Formal adoption of the executive naming convention in official documents and simultaneous passage of the legislative bill.", "facts_supported": true, "key_assumption": "Executive communication terms will overlap legally with legislative definitions in banned tech bills.", "lift_eligible": true, "ordinary_reading": "Donald Trump announced renaming AI to 'super intelligence' in official communications, while Bernie Sanders and Greg Casar introduced a bill to ban 'artificial superintelligence'.", "plain_claim": "The US executive branch's announcement to rename AI 'super intelligence' in official communications coincides with legislative attempts to ban 'artificial superintelligence', leading to conflicting government terminology.", "status": "supported_inference", "uncertainty_preserved": true}, "text": "The executive announcement to rename artificial intelligence 'super intelligence' in US official communications coincides with legislative efforts to ban 'artificial superintelligence', creating conflicting terminology across government branches.", "type": "cross_event", "weakest": "identifying control points and actor constraints", "widely_expected": false}, {"band": "weak or generic", "corroboration": [], "derivation": "derived", "detail": "", "dimensions": {"actor_specificity": 1, "decisio