cies could be functionally paralyzed by conflicting nomenclature mandates.", "watch_signal": "US federal procurement offices issuing guidance memos temporarily halting AI acquisitions due to terminology compliance uncertainties.", "why_not_obvious": "Most observers treat the executive rebranding as mere political rhetoric and the legislative ban as targeting future sci-fi capabilities, missing the immediate statutory gridlock created when both branches mandate conflicting legal treatments for the exact same phrase."}, {"actor_move_basis": "F16", "alternative_explanation": "The Australian health website had exceptionally poor, outdated cybersecurity that failed to catch a standard scraping intrusion, and modern endpoint detection systems can easily identify AI agents.", "anomaly_or_trigger": "In 2019, the victim detected a hack and the FBI captured the attacker; in 2024, the Australian government only realized it was breached because the AI vendor admitted it three months later.", "countermove_basis": "F17", "critic_scores": {"falsifiability": 2, "mechanism_depth": 2, "mental_model_change": 2, "strategic_consequence": 2, "surprise_nonobviousness": 2}, "critic_total": 10, "evidence_ids": ["EVID-C2A4F05609A8DF3032E36EDE", "EVID-16112B7415C6987DC46B214D", "EVID-963B19A140154B53009736B0"], "evolution_note": "Merged B1H3, B1H7, and B2H3 to create a unified thesis on 'Cyber Discovery Inversion'. Strengthened the contrast with the 2019 baseline (H1) to demonstrate the shift in the control point.", "fact_ids": ["F7", "F16", "H1"], "falsifier": "State cybersecurity agencies begin independently detecting and blocking autonomous AI agent web-scraping incursions without relying on vendor notification.", "field_checks": {"actor_move_basis": "unsupported", "countermove_basis": "unsupported", "leverage": "unsupported", "leverage_alternatives": "unsupported", "leverage_asymmetry": "unsupported", "likely_actor_move": "supported", "likely_countermove": "inference_supported"}, "from_us