lly blind.", "insight_id": "LAB-EV2", "insight_type": "prospective", "mechanism": {"description": "The EU implements severe 3% global turnover fines for AI incidents -> AI providers prioritize forensic reviews and compliance reporting to satisfy EU mandates -> Incident discovery and reporting for jurisdictions lacking similar financial teeth (like Australia) is delayed by months."}, "metadata": {"lens": "regulatory arbitrage or policy feedback", "novel_proposition": "Global AI safety incidents are currently reported based on the financial severity of the jurisdiction's penalties rather than the technical severity of the incident or local 12-to-72 hour mandates.", "origin": "strategic-hypothesis-lab-v1.6-blind-user-hypotheses", "why_not_obvious": "An unprecedented AI hack on a government network should theoretically trigger an immediate maximum-priority alert; the 3-month delay reveals that AI model telemetry review is a bottlenecked resource allocated by compliance risk."}, "premises": [{"evidence_ids": ["EVID-C2A4F05609A8DF3032E36EDE"], "premise_id": "LAB-P-F7", "premise_type": "factual", "text": "(At the UN Wednesday Australian Prime Minister Anthony Albanese complained it took three months for OpenAI to then alert Australia's government about the breach, Bloomberg reports .)"}, {"evidence_ids": ["EVID-65CFAEF5390DEF6D131BE273"], "premise_id": "LAB-P-F11", "premise_type": "factual", "text": "Article 55 of the AI Act has obliged providers of general-purpose models with systemic risk to run adversarial testing, assess risk at union level and report serious incidents without undue delay since August 2025."}, {"evidence_ids": ["EVID-52B4FF635215A384AF63E0FF", "EVID-0476EACE53022E410008ABA8", "EVID-697F5CA02E3A1BA05D6F8242"], "premise_id": "LAB-P-F12", "premise_type": "factual", "text": "The European Union has required them since August 2025, and since 2 August this year the Commission has been able to fine a model provider 3% of worldwide turnover."}, {"evidence_ids": ["EVID-7F245C8DCFCBC6762E9746F4", "EVID-86552ACB7912E78EFB41C631"], "premise_id": "LAB-P-F19", "premise_type": "factual", "text": "Within these organisations, if you become aware that a critical cyber security incident has occurred or is occurring, AND the incident has had, or is having, a significant impact on the availability of your asset, you must notify ACSC within 12 hours after you become aware of the incident."}, {"evidence_ids": ["EVID-86552ACB7912E78EFB41C631", "EVID-7F245C8DCFCBC6762E9746F4"], "premise_id": "LAB-P-F20", "premise_type": "factual", "text": "If you become aware that a cyber security incident has occurred or is occurring, AND the incident has had, is having, or is likely to have, a relevant impact on your asset, you must notify ACSC within 72 hours after you become aware of the incident."}], "second_order_effect": "Mid-tier nations will be forced to rapidly adopt European-style, revenue-based extraterritorial fine models simply to secure timely intelligence on their own domestic cyber breaches.", "supporting_evidence_ids": ["EVID-C2A4F05609A8DF3032E36EDE", "EVID-65CFAEF5390DEF6D131BE273", "EVID-52B4FF635215A384AF63E0FF", "EVID-7F245C8DCFCBC6762E9746F4", "EVID-86552ACB7912E78EFB41C631", "EVID-0476EACE53022E410008ABA8", "EVID-697F5CA02E3A1BA05D6F8242"]}, "seed_evidence_ids": ["EVID-C2A4F05609A8DF3032E36EDE", "EVID-65CFAEF5390DEF6D131BE273", "EVID-52B4FF635215A384AF63E0FF", "EVID-7F245C8DCFCBC6762E9746F4", "EVID-86552ACB7912E78EFB41C631", "EVID-0476EACE53022E410008ABA8", "EVID-697F5CA02E3A1BA05D6F8242"], "source_documents": {}, "version": "hypothesis-evidence-v1.1"}, {"as_of": "2026-10-23T07:03:04.642892+00:00", "assessment": {"completeness": "incomplete", "families": {"challenge": {"blockers": ["analogical_mechanism: a fetched source could not be reviewed", "feasibility: a fetched source could not be reviewed"], "limitations": ["alternative_explanation: a found source could not be fetched", "alternative_explanation: gdelt: RATE_LIMITED", "alte