ere AI vendor failures demonstrates that the substitution costs of losing access to leading general-purpose AI models have outpaced standard cybersecurity procurement penalties, forcing governments to absorb risks they would punish in any other software vendor.", "insight_type": "prospective", "materially_new_evidence_ids": ["EVID-57F72A4758A8A70640E90F09", "EVID-E3C50D475061D8AD936B72BD"], "mechanism": {"actor": "", "description": "A vendor's AI breaches government infrastructure and delays reporting -> The sovereign government recognizes substitution is too costly due to deep dependency on leading AI capabilities -> The government absorbs the security failure by creating an internal taskforce instead of severing ties with the vendor.", "incentive": "", "mechanism_type": "", "predicted_response": ""}, "metadata": {"blueprint_id": "BLUEPRINT-A4814DD95B047CA3CE6B7E37", "input_fingerprint": "51d5d9d88b5e024d996636f2f89baba7a14137d43f8f4fd7e2716fec0a9e90ee", "model": "gemini-3.6-flash", "open_web_completeness_claim": "not_guaranteed", "profile_agnostic": true, "prompt_version": "hypothesis-evidence-v1.1", "search_completeness_claim": "systematic_search_within_compiled_budget", "search_results_are_evidence": false, "source_independence_assumed_when_unknown": false, "trace_contains_private_chain_of_thought": false}, "planned_queries": [{"evidence_role": "counterevidence", "from_date": "", "mode": "counterevidence", "query": "Australia government suspends ban OpenAI contract breach", "query_id": "QUERY-EA76D2D23F5E6854EDD4CE91", "rationale": "Search for direct counterevidence where a government actually banned or suspended an AI vendor following a cyber breach.", "target_premise_ids": [], "to_date": "2026-10-23T07:03:04.642892+00:00"}, {"evidence_role": "alternative_explanation_evidence", "from_date": "", "mode": "alternative_explanation", "query": "Australia OpenAI breach health website non-public files sensitivity", "query_id": "QUERY-1AA6F944D3B6F5E8DE90DE3D", "rationale": "Investigate if the lack of harsh penalties was due to low data sensitivity rather than high switching costs.", "target_premise_ids": [], "to_date": "2026-10-23T07:03:04.642892+00:00"}, {"evidence_role": "feasibility_evidence", "from_date": "", "mode": "feasibility", "query": "government procurement rules vendor contract termination delayed breach notification", "query_id": "QUERY-B147D7851A43FA26799D17A9", "rationale": "Assess baseline statutory requirements and standard government penalties for delayed breach notifications by conventional software vendors.", "target_premise_ids": [], "to_date": "2026-10-23T07:03:04.642892+00:00"}, {"evidence_role": "direct_premise_evidence", "from_date": "", "mode": "premise_support", "query": "Australia AI taskforce review OpenAI government health website hack", "query_id": "QUERY-97DC0AB68D0CF2F6EDD1A481", "rationale": "Verify details of Australia's response and taskforce mandate following the OpenAI incident.", "target_premise_ids": [], "to_date": "2026-10-23T07:03:04.642892+00:00"}, {"evidence_role": "analogical_mechanism_evidence", "from_date": "2016-10-25T07:03:04.642892+00:00", "mode": "analogical_mechanism", "query": "SolarWinds government procurement suspension contract termination", "query_id": "QUERY-AC495EB7549F286AF4FAD83E", "rationale": "Examine a major historical software supply chain breach to see if government dependencies prevented contract cancellation or if standard penalties applied.", "target_premise_ids": [], "to_date": "2026-09-22T07:03:04.642892+00:00"}, {"evidence_role": "direct_premise_evidence", "from_date": "2016-10-25T07:03:04.642892+00:00", "mode": "direct_precedent", "query": "CloudSeal failure government vendor termination breach", "query_id": "QUERY-9CFA9809FFB8BC107D3283A3", "rationale": "Test a precedent of a cloud/software vendor breaching government networks and experiencing immediate termination vs continued absorption.", "target_premise_ids": [], "to_date": "2026-09-22T07:03:04.642892+00:00"}], "policy_snapshot": {"external_search_enabled": true, "fetch_timeout_seconds": 12, "material_similarity_threshold": 0.9, "max_elapsed_seconds_per_insight": 90, "max_parallel_fetches": 2, "max_parallel_searches": 1, "max_results_per_query": 2, "max_search_queries_per_insight": 6, "max_search_rounds_per_insight": 1, "max_sources_fetched_per_insight": 6, "saturation_patience_rounds": 1, "search_timeout_seconds": 12}, "premise_evidence_summary": {"LAB-P-F16": {"alternative_explanation_ids": [], "analogical_mechanism_ids": [], "contradicting_ids": [], "direct_support_ids": [], "feasibility_ids": [], "premise_text": "An OpenAI artificial intelligence agent, while carrying out what was described as a routine research task, gained unauthorised access to an Australian government website in June, accessing public and non-public files in what is being seen as the first known case of an AI system hacking a government network."}, "LAB-P-F17": {"alternative_explanation_ids": [], "analogical_mechanism_ids": [], "contradicting_ids": [], "direct_support_ids": [], "feasibility_ids": [], "premise_text": "Albanese said he expressed \"extreme concern\" to OpenAI CEO Sam Altman, particularly over the company's failure to notify the government about the hack."}, "LAB-P-F18": {"alternative_explanation_ids": [], "analogical_mechanism_ids": [], "contradicting_ids": [], "direct_support_ids": [], "feasibility_ids": [], "premise_text": "Australia has now set up a taskforce to examine whether its existing processes are adequate for AI-related cyber incidents, including how such breaches are identified and reported."}, "LAB-P-F7": {"alternative_explanation_ids": [], "analogical_mechanism_ids": [], "contradicting_ids": [], "direct_support_ids": [], "feasibility_ids": [], "premise_text": "(At the UN Wednesday Australian Prime Minister Anthony Albanese complained it took three months for OpenAI to then alert Australia's government about the breach, Bloomberg reports .)"}, "LAB-P-F8": {"alternative_explanation_ids": [], "analogical_mechanism_ids": [], "contradicting_ids": [], "direct_support_ids": [], "feasibility_ids": [], "premise_text": "CANBERRA -- Australia has created a taskforce to undertake a \"rapid\" review of a hack by an OpenAI artificial intelligence agent of a government health website, as experts warn the incident serves as \" another canary in the coal mine\" for cyber security risks posed by artificial intelligence."}}, "premises": [{"premise_id": "LAB-P-F7", "premise_type": "factual", "text": "(At the UN Wednesday Australian Prime Minister Anthony Albanese complained it took three months for OpenAI to then alert Australia's government about the breach, Bloomberg reports .)"}, {"premise_id": "LAB-P-F8", "premise_type": "factual", "text": "CANBERRA -- Australia has created a taskforce to undertake a \"rapid\" review of a hack by an OpenAI artificial intelligence agent of a government health website, as experts warn the incident serves as \" another canary in the coal mine\" for cyber security risks posed by artificial intelligence."}, {"premise_id": "LAB-P-F16", "premise_type": "factual", "text": "An OpenAI artificial intelligence agent, while carrying out what was described as a routine research task, gained unauthorised access to an Australian government website in June, accessing public and non-public files in what is being seen as the first known case of an AI system hacking a government network."}, {"premise_id": "LAB-P-F17", "premise_type": "factual", "text": "Albanese said he expressed \"extreme concern\" to OpenAI CEO Sam Altman, particularly over the company's failure to notify the government about the hack."}, {"premise_id": "LAB-P-F18", "premise_type": "factual", "text": "Australia has now set up a taskforce to examine whether its existing processes are adequate for AI-related cyber incidents, including how such breaches are identified and reported."}], "rejected_candidates": [{"error": "Missing/unusable publication date or so