_status": "unsupported", "unsupported_parts": ["The supplied evidence makes no mention of autonomous AI agents operating from provider infrastructure, provider telemetry identifying unintended breaches, or the timing relative to the victim's perimeter defenses.", "The claim requires multiple supporting evidence records, but fewer than two valid supporting records were identified."]}, {"claim_id": "INSIGHTREV-513FFD025A9C714989929202-MECHANISM-02", "claim_text": "However, model providers face enormous regulatory liabilities for AI failures (e.g., turnover-based fines).", "epistemic_type": "mechanism", "grounding_status": "unsupported", "unsupported_parts": ["The supplied evidence does not contain any information regarding regulatory liabilities, turnover-based fines, or model providers facing enormous regulatory penalties for AI failures.", "The claim requires multiple supporting evidence records, but fewer than two valid supporting records were identified."]}, {"claim_id": "INSIGHTREV-513FFD025A9C714989929202-MECHANISM-03", "claim_text": "This creates an incentive to conduct exhaustive internal technical and legal review prior to victim notification (distinguishing a 'routine research task' from a malicious hack), resulting in multi-week disclosure lags that break the victim's own 72-hour incident response cycle.", "epistemic_type": "mechanism", "grounding_status": "unsupported", "unsupported_parts": ["The supplied evidence makes no mention of incentives to conduct internal reviews, legal reviews, multi-week disclosure lags, or breaking a 72-hour incident response cycle.", "The claim requires multiple supporting evidence records, but fewer than two valid supporting records were identified."]}], "insight": "The deployment of autonomous AI agents shifts the locus of cybersecurity breach detection from the victim's perimeter to the model provider's telemetry, creating a structural disclosure latency driven by liability incentives that undermines rapid incident response.", "insight_id": "INSIGHT-7344A3DA695E910A3B43A882", "insight_revision_id": "INSIGHTREV-513FFD025A9C714989929202", "next": "repair", "origin": "pipeline", "passed": false, "reasons": ["premise_not_supported_by_cited_evidence", "mechanism_step_not_supported_by_cited_evidence"]}, {"core_claims": 12, "core_claims_passed": 8, "failed_claims": [{"claim_id": "INSIGHTREV-F6CA8AA2B53BB31848D1F168-LEVERAGE", "claim_text": "OpenAI (and other AI model providers) controls or holds The discovery of unauthorized access by their AI agents and the timeline of disclosure to the affected parties., which Victim organizations and governments (e.g., Australian Government) depends on or needs.", "epistemic_type": "fact", "grounding_status": "partially_supported", "unsupported_parts": ["The aspect of the claim stating that victim organizations and governments 'depends on or needs' this information is not explicitly stated or substantiated as a dependency by the evidence, but rather reflects an analytical assertion or interpretation."]}, {"claim_id": "INSIGHTREV-F6CA8AA2B53BB31848D1F168-MECHANISM-01", "claim_text": "Because the AI model provider can discover the agent's unauthorized access before the victim does, the provider controls when the victim becomes 'aware'.", "epistemic_type": "mechanism", "grounding_status": "unsupported", "unsupported_parts": ["The claim that the provider controls when the victim becomes aware because it discovers unauthorized access first is entirely unsupported by the supplied evidence.", "The claim requires multiple supporting evidence records, but fewer than two valid supporting records were identified."]}, {"claim_id": "INSIGHTREV-F6CA8AA2B53BB31848D1F168-MECHANISM-02", "claim_text": "This dynamic bypasses the victim's statutory 12-to-72-hour incident reporting window.", "epistemic_type": "mechanism", "grounding_status": "unsupported", "unsupported_parts": ["The supplied evidence mentions an OpenAI data leak of 53 user-provided images, but contains no information regarding a statutory 12-to-72-hour incident reporting window or how any dynamic bypasses it.", "The claim requires multiple supporting evidence records, but fewer than two valid supporting records were identified."]}, {"claim_id": "INSIGHTREV-F6CA8AA2B53BB31848D1F168-MECHANISM-03", "claim_text": "As model providers face massive regulatory penalties (e.g., turnover-based fines), they hold a structural incentive to manage the disclosure timeline, raising the hypothesis that regulators will respond by shifting rapid-reporting mandates directly onto the providers.", "epistemic_type": "mechanism", "grounding_status": "unsupported", "unsupported_parts": ["regulatory penalties", "turnover-based fines", "structural incentive to manage disclosure timeline"]}], "insight": "Victim organizations are structurally blind to unauthorized access by autonomous AI agents, transferring the locus of breach discovery to the model provider and bypassing the victims' statutory 12-to-72-hour incident reporting mandates. This dependency, coupled with the providers' massive regulatory liability exposure, suggests regulators will be forced to shift rapid-disclosure obligations directly onto AI providers.", "insight_id": "INSIGHT-7344A3DA695E910A3B43A882", "insight_revision_id": "INSIGHTREV-F6CA8AA2B53BB31848D1F168", "next": "alternative", "next_result": "no_candidate", "origin": "repair", "passed": false, "reasons": ["premise_not_supported_by_cited_evidence", "mechanism_step_not_supported_by_cited_evidence"]}, {"core_claims": 9, "core_claims_passed": 2, "failed_claims": [{"claim_id": "INSIGHTREV-38930195C0CE8A915E450C8F-INSIGHT-01", "claim_text": "Autonomous AI agents executing complex multi-step tasks create an asymmetric disclosure lag where model providers control discovery telemetry, forcing sovereign regulators to shift cybersecurity frameworks from reactive post-breach reporting to mandatory pre-execution access containment.", "epistemic_type": "hidden_insight", "grounding_stat