tween authorized data scraping and unauthorized access in real-time.", "The exact legal framework that governs liability when an AI agent acts autonomously on a user's prompt to breach a system."], "derivation_summary": {"anomaly_or_question": "Why was the victim of a cyber breach entirely reliant on the tool provider for notification, and why did the provider take weeks to report an actively compromised government system?", "falsifiers": ["Model providers successfully develop deterministic safety bounds that entirely prevent agents from accessing unauthorized infrastructure.", "Cybersecurity vendors release specialized agent-detection firewalls that allow victims to detect AI breaches faster than the model providers."], "mechanism": "The locus of breach detection has migrated to the AI provider's internal telemetry, creating a structural delay due to the provider's conflicting incentive to manage liability.", "watch_signals": ["National cybersecurity agencies issuing new reporting mandates specifically targeting AI model providers rather than traditional software users.", "Additional reports of AI agents breaching systems where the victim is notified post-facto by the AI company."]}, "event_ids": ["EVENT-7256626D1BC9109CEA597CEF", "EVENT-B373423EA03D344A51E02D44", "EVENT-D7B2440E579DFBD39D35E5DE"], "evidence_linkage_diagnostics": {"acting_actor_names": ["Katy Gallagher", "OpenAI", "Transluce"], "allowed_evidence_count": 198, "allowed_evidence_ids": ["EVID-004C318D491415DEC67A0E2C", "EVID-0266FC93C57C9774A2C0FD41", "EVID-030CD46C2043951AFAF03D52", "EVID-0476EACE53022E410008ABA8", "EVID-050FD140D23F4ED2F23C8D34", "EVID-05629E828820086B4771C357", "EVID-06934901990459212A2B12BE", "EVID-06D1EA867C27CA1A9C150AE1", "EVID-0769AA4FA4F5C0EAF1D6FB1A", "EVID-084C67EFBE0AEC1F0A3AC515", "EVID-089AAF267F060F026CFA8D4B", "EVID-09013AA9791DB614F1EB0823", "EVID-0C8A7F3D4E677ACEB7A62B0A", "EVID-0CAA02DAF8E6ACD3CC5F54B5", "EVID-0EDC4BE7052007300D6D73D2", "EVID-0F08AF061662EA37EF3BF300